  "Name": "Brennan1963-ruby-HLH-3L",
  "Source": "E. R. Brennan, \"Multi-Layer All-Dielectric Reflection Filters,\" M.S. thesis (Physics), Polytechnic Institute of Brooklyn (1963), thesis adviser A. Zajac. No doi. - Abstract p. ii; Sec. II.A p. 4; Fig. 1(c), p. 3",
  "Notes": "Three-layer all-dielectric ruby-laser end reflector, ZnS/MgF2/ZnS quarter waves, > 60 % reflectance at 694.3 nm\nSpecification: Reflectance > 60 % at the ruby wavelength 694.3 nm, light incident from inside the ruby, normal incidence.\nReported: Reflectance increases to 62 % at 694.3 nm, normal incidence (p. 4).\nNotes: Fig. 1(c): RUBY | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | AIR, n1 = n3. Ruby assumed n = 1.76 (not printed in the preview). A quarter-wave admittance calculation with the printed indices gives about 64.8 % (65.0 % with n0 = 1.75), not the 62 % printed; reaching 62 % would need n0 ~ 1.94, so the printed 62 % looks like a rounding or arithmetic difference in the thesis. Merit 'Min 0.6' encodes R >= 60 %.\nLayers from Abstract p. ii; Sec. II.A p. 4; Fig. 1(c), p. 3; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours R 64.8 % at 694.3 nm; paper R 62.0 % (pp. 2-4). The thesis’s own indices give 64.8 %, not its 62 %; 62 % would need a ruby index near 1.94. The ruby index (1.76) is assumed: the preview pages do not give it.",
